    "created_at": "2019-05-10T15:53:19Z",
    "updated_at": "2019-05-10T15:53:19Z",
    "body": "For folks watching this popular thread, we've just added a [parse JSON into Infra values](https://infra.spec.whatwg.org/#parse-json-into-infra-values) algorithm. This gives you back Infra ordered maps/lists/booleans/numbers/strings/nulls, which your spec can operate on without having to (ab)use JavaScript abstract operations or Web IDL dictionaries.\r\n\r\nYou can see a not-quite-finished usage example of this in a parsing setting in https://github.com/WICG/import-maps/pull/130 ([preview](https://pr-preview.s3.amazonaws.com/WICG/import-maps/pull/130.html#parsing)), or hopefully in a day or two, in https://wicg.github.io/import-maps/.\r\n\r\nI think there is perhaps room for a future JSON schema-based solution for validation, or standardized documentation format for JSON, but for the purpose of specifying processing models, I suspect this is going to be the best way for a while, and will closely match implementations.",
    "author_association": "MEMBER",
    "pin": null,
